  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Sets the KERNAL start address (STAL $c1/$c2) to $6000 and the end address (EAL $ae/$af) to $7f40: the 8000 bitmap bytes."},
    {"at":17,"placement":"line","text":"Sets STAL to $c000 and EAL to $c7d1: the screen colours, the colour RAM and the background colour (2001 bytes). Then copies STAL to the KERNAL pointer $ac/$ad ($fb8e)."},
    {"at":36,"placement":"line","text":"Saves the picture as a Koala file with the file name and device that are set. Opens the file with secondary address 1 ($f3d5) and checks the drive status ($2d2d, drive_status); on an error it jumps to $2c22. Then sends the load address $6000, the bitmap $6000-$7f3f and $c000-$c7d0, and closes the file ($f63f). The STOP key ends the save with C set."},
    {"at":39,"placement":"side","text":"SA = $61: secondary address 1."},
    {"at":56,"placement":"side","text":"LISTEN."},
    {"at":61,"placement":"side","text":"SECOND."},
    {"at":64,"placement":"side","text":"$ac/$ad = STAL ($6000)."},
    {"at":69,"placement":"side","text":"CIOUT: the load address, low byte then high byte."},
    {"at":91,"placement":"line","text":"Sends the bytes from $ac/$ad up to EAL with CIOUT. The STOP key closes the file ($f642), drops the return address and returns from the caller with A = 0 and C set."},
    {"at":91,"placement":"side","text":"C set when $ac/$ad has reached EAL."},
    {"at":121,"placement":"line","text":"Loads a Koala file with the file name and device that are set. Opens the file with secondary address 0 ($f3d5) and checks the drive status ($2d2d, drive_status); on an error it jumps to $2c22. The file's load address is not used: the first 8000 bytes go to the bitmap $6000-$7f3f, the next 2001 bytes to $c000-$c7d0. A read timeout on the first byte gives FILE NOT FOUND ($f704)."},
    {"at":128,"placement":"side","text":"SA = $60: secondary address 0."},
    {"at":145,"placement":"side","text":"TALK."},
    {"at":150,"placement":"side","text":"TKSA."},
    {"at":153,"placement":"side","text":"ACPTR: the low byte of the load address."},
    {"at":156,"placement":"side","text":"STATUS bit 1: read timeout."},
    {"at":162,"placement":"side","text":"ACPTR: the high byte of the load address."},
    {"at":182,"placement":"line","text":"Reads bytes with ACPTR to $ac/$ad up to EAL. After a read timeout (STATUS bit 1) it reads again. The STOP key drops the return address and jumps to $f633 in the KERNAL."},
    {"at":222,"placement":"side","text":"KERNAL error FILE NOT FOUND."}
  ],
